==Battleground==
*3 [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.
*1 [[Malizabeth]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*1 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Archbaron Face]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 1.33 seconds<sup>40f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Kaijin Doge]]s spawn after 2.67 seconds<sup>80f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**6 [[J.J. Jackrabbit]]s spawn after 2.67 seconds<sup>80f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**6 [[Malizabeth]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**1 [[Emperor Warumongar]] spawns after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A very easy stage. Kill J.J.Jackrabbit with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], then stall out Malizabeth until you max out your wallet. You can go all out now; there's genuinely no threat here that isn't overwhelmed by the sheer damage of your [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]] + Courier Cat. The bosses have hardly any pierce too, so [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]] are enough to hold them back. You can forego [[Helmet Cat (Special Cat)|Yellow Nyanko Ranger]] for a better DPS option, as they serve no purpose here.

